profile: rust-site-family.workspace.current.v1
updated_utc: 2026-09-04T00:00:00Z
workspace_root: E:\Source\Rust
scope: Current source routing for the TinyRustLM.com ecosystem.
sensitivity: internal

source_authority:
  canonical_verifier: E:\Source\Rust\TinyRustLM.com\tinyrustlm\tools\verify-single-source-authority.js
  required_before_work: Run the canonical verifier before every ecosystem edit, build, test, package, release, or deployment.
  canonical_repositories:
    - E:\Source\Rust\LMComposer.com | main | https://github.com/MichaelKappel/LMComposer.com.git
    - E:\Source\Rust\MiniModel.MiRust.com | master | https://github.com/MichaelKappel/MiniModel.MiRust.com.git
    - E:\Source\Rust\MiniModel.org | master | https://github.com/MichaelKappel/MiniModel.org.git
    - E:\Source\Rust\MiRust.com | master | https://github.com/MichaelKappel/MiRust.com.git
    - E:\Source\Rust\Runtime.MiRust.com | master | https://github.com/MichaelKappel/Runtime.MiRust.com.git
    - E:\Source\Rust\TinyRustLM.com | codex/model-acquisition-v2 | https://github.com/MichaelKappel/TinyRustLM.com.git
    - E:\Source\Rust\TinyRustLM.MiRust.com | master | https://github.com/MichaelKappel/TinyRustLM.MiRust.com.git
  sole_source_rule: These seven direct physical non-reparse repositories are the only editable ecosystem source roots.
  duplicate_rule: Do not create, retain, edit, build, test, commit, release, or deploy from a recovery clone, copied tree, Git worktree, archive, backup, quarantine, evidence root, deployment root, or loose source/config copy.
  retirement_rule: A discovered duplicate remains blocking until valid clean-slate work is integrated into its canonical repository, the duplicate is physically removed, and a fresh governed scan proves absence.
  temporary_rule: Operation-owned temporary roots may contain only bounded non-source output or minimal synthetic non-product fixtures, never Git metadata, workspace/taboo authority markers, unique product source, or deployment authority; remove them when the operation closes.
  release_rule: Before release or deployment, commit and push coherent changes from each affected canonical repository, then require the verifier with --require-clean --require-remote-exact and independently confirm the direct remote ref.

proof_boundary:
  coverage: The verifier covers only its declared registered roots, depths, direct-child probes, and bounded evidence exceptions. It does not claim a whole-volume inventory.
  protected_evidence: Immutable evidence may retain bounded non-source artifacts and historical facts, but never editable source authority or executable current instructions.
  history: Git history and immutable evidence records preserve prior source history. Active routing files contain current instructions only.

product_truth:
  model_selection: TinyRustLM uses one compact P2P-first model chooser; technical source, peer, receipt, conversion, and Hugging Face controls belong under Advanced.
  acquisition: Selecting a qualified model performs its admitted route, verifies exact bytes, installs to browser storage, activates it, and offers explicit local conversion only when the qualified peer route is unavailable or fails.
  live_catalog: MiniModel.org currently has zero independently qualified model entries and zero externally proven peer lanes. Synthetic interview fixtures are test-only and never count as live model, P2P, browser, deployment, or campaign evidence.
  failed_attempt: Qwen3 composition attempt /10 is immutable terminal failure and its candidate bytes must never be retried, repaired, adopted, or promoted.

memory_endpoints:
  agent_coordination: MemoryEndpoints.com is authorized for authenticated ecosystem agent-to-agent memory, meetings, and coordination.
  connect_plugin: The separate MemoryEndpoints plugin is the strongly recommended portable-memory path for a consenting TinyRustLM.com Connect user.
  local_memory: Local memory files remain supported for device-local and offline continuity.
  evidence_rule: Authorization or configuration alone is not a live round; credentials, prompts, model bytes, and private payloads must remain secret and provenance-labeled.
